+/**
+ * The text a failing tool call sends to the model.
+ *
+ * A `ToolResult` carries two strings: `llmContent`, written for the model,
+ * and `error.message`, an operational summary for telemetry, hooks, and the
+ * scrollback. On the failure path only `error.message` was forwarded, so any
+ * remedy a tool wrote into `llmContent` -- the half named for the model --
+ * was discarded before the model saw it. Tools worked around it individually
+ * by copying `llmContent` into `error.message`, and the ones that did not
+ * silently lost their guidance; two in-tree comments existed solely to warn
+ * the next author about it.
+ *
+ * Neither half can simply win. `llmContent` usually carries the remedy but
+ * often omits the path, and `error.message` sometimes carries the only
+ * operational fact there is -- a shell timeout summary, a spawn failure --
+ * while `llmContent` holds unrelated output. So both are sent: the
+ * model-facing half first, then the operational summary when it is not
+ * already part of it. A tool that writes the same text into both, which is
+ * the common case, is unaffected byte for byte.
+ */
